{
  "summary": "This experiment tested transformer aggregation in place of avgpool, changing only the aggregation strategy while holding scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, and weighted fusion fixed relative to the prior best (llm_summary_009, acc ~0.706). In this clean single-variable comparison, transformer aggregation improved validation accuracy to ~0.725 (F1 ~0.685), a gain of ~0.019, reversing the prior finding under PCA-2000 where transformer underperformed avgpool by ~0.07 and suggesting that attention-based aggregation interacts favorably with the learned nonlinear 200-dim latent features of scvi_n200. It remains uncertain whether this modest gain is stable across runs, whether further transformer hyperparameter tuning could yield additional improvement, and whether other unexplored dimensions (e.g., alternative fusion mechanisms or encoder variants) could build on this new best configuration."
}

